 "summary": "Mostly no. On 1h and 4h, three uses did no better than random candles on BTC, ETH and SOL: buying more than 10% under the 100-bar high, buying the cross down through 10%, and shorting within 5% of the high. The one result that holds up is on 1h only. Entries more than 20% under the 100-bar high beat random entries by 1.51% after 20 candles, and that gap came from uptrends.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Buying a deep drawdown (more than 20% under the 100-bar high)",
   "verdict": "edge",
   "text": "On 1h, price rose 1.51% more than after random candles over the next 20 candles, against a luck band that tops out at 0.56%. On 4h and daily the same level showed nothing."
  },
  {
   "use": "Buying a 10% dip (level, 10% to 20% band, or cross down through 10%)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "On 1h and 4h, none of these did better than random entries. On daily the band and the cross also land inside the luck band, and the level has too few separate moves to judge."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting near the high (within 5% of the 100-bar high)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "On 1h, 4h and daily this did no better than random entries, in uptrends or in downtrends."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, entries more than 20% under the 100-bar high gave 4,022 entries in 183 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 1.51% ahead of random entries, and the luck band runs from -0.44% to 0.56%. The result holds without its strongest stretch, 54 entries on Sep 16–18, 2020, and it also shows at 10 and 50 candles. At 100 candles it is back to chance. ETH was ahead by 0.98% and SOL by 1.52%. BTC reached this depth in only 21 separate moves, which is too few to judge.",
  "The 1h result comes from uptrends. When the pair closed above its 200-day SMA, these entries were 2.4% ahead of random uptrend candles, above a band that ends at 0.92%. In downtrends they were 0.51% ahead, which is inside the band, so they showed nothing. On 4h the same level landed at -0.04% and on daily at -0.65%, both inside their luck bands.",
  "On 1h, entries more than 10% under the 100-bar high happened about seven times as often as entries more than 20% under it. They showed nothing: 0.15% ahead of random, inside a band of -0.14% to 0.24%. Uptrends gave 0.35% and downtrends -0.12%, and both are inside their bands. On 4h the level gave -0.09%, and the 10% to 20% band gave -0.07% on 1h. On daily the 10% level has only 20 separate moves, under the 30 needed to judge it.",
  "The cross down through 10% came out at 0.03% on 1h, which is chance. In 1h downtrends it reached 0.34%, just above a band that ends at 0.31%. That came from 3 entries on Feb 27–28, 2022, and without them it falls back to chance. On 1h BTC the cross looked worse than random, at -0.34%, but only because of signals on Aug 2–4, 2024. On daily, downtrend crossings add up to only 6 separate moves, which is too few to judge.",
  "On 1h, being within 5% of the 100-bar high happened on 87,786 candles. A short from those candles came out at 0.06%, inside a band of -0.05% to 0.09%. On 4h it gave -0.14% and on daily 0.49%, both chance. Neither regime moved it out of the band on 1h or 4h. On daily, downtrend entries form a single separate move, so they were never judged. Price near its recent high told you nothing about the next 20 candles, in either direction.",
  "For a long DCA bot on 1h, use the drawdown of more than 20% below the 100-bar high as a filter beside your other start conditions, not as the trigger on its own. Pair it with a trend filter, because in downtrends it showed nothing. The gap was gone by 100 candles, so a take profit that tends to fill within 50 candles fits this shape better than one that waits longer. The 10% levels and the near-high short add nothing on these pairs, and your DCA orders and take profit do the work there. When it fails: in downtrends, and on 4h or daily, the deep drawdown was a coin flip."
 ],
